# =============================================================================
# quick.env - switch any command to the QUICK run profile
# =============================================================================
# WHAT IT IS
#   An "env file": settings loaded as environment variables when a command
#   starts. uv loads it with --env-file, and the same command works on
#   Windows, Mac and Linux:
#
#     uv run --env-file quick.env pipeline.py                  quick training run
#     uv run --env-file quick.env uvicorn api.main:app         serve the quick model
#     uv run --env-file quick.env simulate_traffic.py --drift  quick simulated users
#     uv run --env-file quick.env monitor.py                   quick drift check
#
#   Without --env-file quick.env, every command uses the FULL profile.
#
# WHAT QUICK MODE DOES
#   Runs the whole pipeline end to end on a 20,000-row stratified sample, with
#   lighter settings, in seconds. Use it to check everything works before a
#   full run. Its outputs (data/quick/, models_quick/, logs, an MLflow
#   experiment named diabetes-risk-quick) are fully separate from production.
#   All quick settings live in src/config.py, next to their full values.
# =============================================================================
RUN_PROFILE=quick
